# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp

# Python cache (from research scripts, if re-run)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Full-catalog CVE mirror (built by cve_reference_builder.py mirror/mirror-update) --
# hundreds of MB at full scale, local-only cache, never committed. The small curated
# execution-plan/tools/data/cve_reference.json (built by fetch/fetch-list) IS committed.
execution-plan/tools/data/cve_mirror.json

# Local bulk Nessus plugin import (built by nessus_reference_builder.py import-bulk from a
# plugin feed the user obtained themselves via their own free Nessus Essentials activation
# code). Unlike cve_mirror.json above, this is NOT a redistributable public mirror -- it is
# derived from Tenable's licensed plugin content and only exists locally if the user built it
# themselves from their own feed download. Never committed. The small curated
# execution-plan/tools/data/nessus_reference.json (built by fetch/fetch-list) IS committed.
execution-plan/tools/data/nessus_mirror.json

# Role assignments captured by execution-plan/tools/start_here.py -- who holds each
# JSIG role is program-specific/named data, out of scope for this unclassified,
# general-framework reference repo (see root README's Scope note). Local-only.
execution-plan/tools/data/role_assignments.local.json

# NVD API key entered interactively via start_here.py's CVE step -- a personal
# credential, never committed. Set the NVD_API_KEY environment variable instead
# if you'd rather not have it touch disk at all.
execution-plan/tools/data/nvd_api_key.local.txt

# Intake drop-zones are personal, local staging areas -- only the folder
# structure (.gitkeep) and example files belong in git. Whatever a user
# drops in locally to build their own STIG/CVE/Nessus reference databases
# should never get committed (see: the Windows 11 STIG XCCDF that got
# accidentally committed to stig_intake/ on 2026-07-18, since removed).
execution-plan/tools/stig_intake/*
!execution-plan/tools/stig_intake/.gitkeep
execution-plan/tools/cve_intake/*
!execution-plan/tools/cve_intake/.gitkeep
!execution-plan/tools/cve_intake/cve_list.example.txt
execution-plan/tools/nessus_intake/*
!execution-plan/tools/nessus_intake/.gitkeep
!execution-plan/tools/nessus_intake/plugin_list.example.txt

# Rendered MRC handbook PDFs (execution-plan/tools/render_mrc_handbook.py output) -- large
# regenerable binary artifacts derived purely from the committed .md cards, and purely from
# the DOCX in the same folder (soffice --convert-to pdf). The .docx handbooks ARE committed
# (see execution-plan/mrc-cards/*/MRC-HANDBOOK-*.docx) as the primary distributable
# deliverable; only the PDF companion stays out of source control. Never hand-edit either --
# run render_mrc_handbook.py to regenerate the .docx, then soffice to get your own .pdf.
execution-plan/mrc-cards/*/MRC-HANDBOOK-*.pdf

# Session handoff notes -- local-only status snapshots written between agent sessions to
# resume work quickly. Never committed; purely a scratch file for continuity.
status.md
